{"skill":{"slug":"excel-xlsx","displayName":"Excel / XLSX"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1773243166499,"changelog":"Tightened formula anchoring, recalculation, and model traceability after a stricter external spreadsheet audit.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6960,"sha256":"52421d9fba8fdb64124416c450849434f3639e7b95249ce10fecd209aa90f038","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1870,"sha256":"1ca3fbe81c9663f3b852a7a011e5e884d3f4f9b4ba198792cb4fe2a368eb1118","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":false,"checkedAt":1789056378185,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c1514cee492f3b155e7965cf29dd0ba5fd522b2bad9a39f11c496323bb0958db","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c1514cee492f3b155e7965cf29dd0ba5fd522b2bad9a39f11c496323bb0958db","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: excel-xlsx\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill bundle consists of metadata and a comprehensive set of instructions (SKILL.md) for an AI agent to handle Excel/XLSX files using best practices. It focuses on data integrity, formula preservation, and formatting standards while warning against common pitfalls like date-system bugs and data type mangling. No executable code, data exfiltration attempts, or malicious prompt injections were found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162621617},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":7,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789056378185},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Excel workbook guidance skill with no bundled code, hidden persistence, or credential handling.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill may lead an agent to read or write user-provided workbook files, which is proportionate to its Excel editing purpose and does not request broad local indexing, credentials, or network access.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file with metadata requiring no binaries; optional related-skill installation is explicitly conditioned on user confirmation.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are scoped to choosing appropriate spreadsheet tools and avoiding common Excel corruption risks; they do not attempt prompt hijacking, hidden automation, data exfiltration, or unrelated actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No scripts, background workers, services, memory writes, privilege escalation, or persistent hooks are present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to create, inspect, and edit Excel/XLSX files, and the instructions are aligned with spreadsheet handling, formula preservation, dates, formatting, and workbook review.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you want spreadsheet-specific guidance for Excel files. As with any workbook-editing skill, review changes to important financial or business spreadsheets before relying on them, because formula or formatting edits can affect results.","findings":"[EA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited 'without checking' text is a warning about copying formulas unsafely, not an instruction to autonomously perform destructive actions; the surrounding artifact repeatedly instructs verification and review before delivery.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789056378185}}}}}